  "slug": "artist:ugk",
  "name": "UGK",
  "editorial_article": "Formed in 1987 in Port Arthur, Texas, by Chad \"Pimp C\" Butler and Bernard \"Bun B\" Freeman, UGK defined a pivotal era of Southern hip-hop. The duo gained national prominence with their 1996 studio album Ridin' Dirty, which received RIAA Gold certification. Their discography spans six studio albums, including the 2007 double album Underground Kingz. Beyond their own releases, they are known for numerous collaborations, appearing on tracks like Master P's \"Break 'Em Off Somethin'\" and Big Boi's \"Gossip.\" Their legacy remains influential in Texas music, marked by frequent appearances on soundtracks for films such as Menace II Society and I'm Bout It.",
